WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:00.400
All right.

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:00.867
Listening to

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:01.501
President Biden

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.836
there, speaking from the Oval Office,

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:04.671
his first address from the Oval Office

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:05.972
as president,

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:08.008
touting the passage of that bipartisan

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.376
bill to raise the debt

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:10.410
ceiling interestingly

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:11.211
calling out Speaker

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:13.213
McCarthy by name,

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:15.015
crediting him with operating in

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:16.182
good faith,

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.751
saying that the Republican negotiators

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:18.585
kept their word.

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:19.519
Plenty of compliments

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:21.421
for those Republicans.

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:23.690
Also mentioning Mitch McConnell.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:24.224
He did.

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:25.959
Interestingly in all of this,

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:28.194
though, make sure to tout something

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.462
Democrats really wanted

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:30.630
and that really had cause

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:31.297
many Republicans

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:32.365
who opposed this to go ahead

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:33.933
with that opposition with their vote.

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:35.502
And that was to tout

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:36.336
some of the additional

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:38.171
funding for the IRS.

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:39.873
So our panel is back with me now.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.941
Phil Mattingly, just to ask you.

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:42.442
Your sense

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:44.144
when you heard that obviously,

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:44.611
you know,

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:45.345
he was talking about

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:45.979
how we protected

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:47.347
Social Security

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:48.048
and Medicare,

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:50.050
those important things for seniors.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.451
But he did make a point

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:51.851
of both

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:53.319
complimenting the Republicans,

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:55.488
which is a double edged sword and

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:57.223
touting the IRS.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:00:59.392
Yeah, Erin,

00:00:59.392 --> 00:00:59.759
you know,

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:01.261
I was just exchanging text back

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:01.694
and forth

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.696
with a Republican member of Congress

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:05.999
who said there was nothing new in here.

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:07.967
And my response was exactly.

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:09.335
And while that might seem

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:10.170
a little bit

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.004
strange,

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:12.138
given the fact it's an Oval Office

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:13.573
address, given the fact it's a Friday,

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.075
this has been the president's

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:16.810
theory of the case for years.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:17.777
It was what his theory

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.345
the case was during the campaign.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.580
And I think you listen

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.982
to this speech understanding

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:25.018
where his priorities were.

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:26.553
What he has long been focused on,

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:26.853
and I think to

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:27.187
some degree,

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:29.255
what his message is and will be over

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.925
the course of the next 15, 16 months.

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:33.626
Yes. Compromise is important.

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:35.095
Bring down the temperature is important.

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:36.062
Being willing to negotiate

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:37.831
is important on policy

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:39.532
in order to govern, not on principles.

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:39.933
And by that

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:41.734
I mean his focus on the fact Medicare

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.470
and Social Security were kept out.

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:44.003
To your point

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:46.172
about the legislative priorities

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:47.440
and the legislative wins that he had

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:47.640
in those

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:48.775
first two years, ensuring

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:49.442
that those

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.111
were largely left untouched

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:51.978
except for the shifting

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:53.546
of some of that IRS funding.

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:54.914
But making very clear

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:56.249
that the willingness and ability

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:57.617
to talk to Republicans

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:59.285
and get bipartisan agreement

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:00.220
was important to know

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.155
there wasn't any dramatic new development

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:03.356
or announcement

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:04.858
or policy in these remarks.

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:06.159
This was a framing speech,

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:07.627
a last word speech

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:08.895
And I think very much a

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:09.829
this is the president's

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:11.097
theory of the case speech,

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:12.265
whether you think it's new or not.

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:12.866
Right. Right.

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:13.867
Well, in theory of the case

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:14.300
is, of course,

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.135
what he's doing as he's

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:16.870
now right up for reelection, right

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:18.872
this is a campaign we know.

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:20.340
How do you think it goes over

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.474
with Speaker McCarthy,

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:22.842
with Senator McConnell,

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:24.444
when the president had states

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:26.012
calls them out

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:27.180
to compliment them,

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:27.881
to say

00:02:27.881 --> 00:02:28.615
they operated

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:29.282
in good faith,

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:31.651
to say that they kept their word?

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:33.453
Do those things

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:34.654
are those things good for them?

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:36.556
Are those things just just unfortunately,

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:37.690
in the world that we live in now

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:38.258
just bad?

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:41.227
Erin, they are what they are

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:42.629
because it's no change

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:42.896
to who

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:44.497
Biden has been all along

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:46.533
from the time that he took office to now

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:48.801
He hasn't changed his tone at all

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.336
when he talks about Republicans.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:51.771
He starts out by thanking them,

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:52.505
complimenting them.

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:53.173
So to your point

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:55.008
about this being a campaign now,

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.075
I haven't seen Biden

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:57.610
take on campaign mode

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.712
compared to his predecessor, Trump,

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:00.847
who would sort of

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:01.481
speak about

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:03.149
whatever the substance of the day

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:06.019
was, policy in a way that was moody

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:07.353
Trump would,

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:08.388
you know, take a different tone

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:09.222
every time.

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:11.191
Biden, what you see is what you get.

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:13.126
And there was a lot to bite off tonight

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:14.494
in tonight's remarks.

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:16.362
He really ran the gamut

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:18.531
talking from the deficit

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:19.499
cutting spending.

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:20.400
Of course, complimenting

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.834
those Republicans, as you said.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.169
But a couple things I liked.

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:23.836
I like that

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:25.805
he used that line

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:26.873
I said, no,

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:28.141
I think that was pretty strong.

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:30.176
He wanted to show that he's still here,

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:31.411
he's still in command,

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:33.780
and he's able to do the job cognitively.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:34.948
That's really big.

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:36.683
But the other part that I didn't love

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:37.483
because I don't think this

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:38.685
is going to have an impact

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:40.186
when we go to the grocery store shelves,

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:41.788
what do we see or what do we see?

00:03:41.788 --> 00:03:43.156
He talked about inflation

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:44.157
slowing for the 10th

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:45.458
for the 10th straight month.

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:45.825
Yeah.

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:47.427
I don't feel that in everyday life.

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:48.661
Republicans certainly don't.

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:49.295
So for

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:50.330
whatever this was

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.497
him taking a victory lap

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:53.132
and certainly this was historic.

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:54.968
This was still an 11th hour

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:56.102
governing situation.

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:58.238
So I see Biden as having maintain

00:03:58.238 --> 00:03:59.072
the status quo

00:03:59.072 --> 00:03:59.839
and not really

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:01.507
have brought the claws out tonight.

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:03.309
What do you think, Jeff Zeleny? Was this?

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:05.378
Was this a taste of a

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:06.879
Biden campaign speech or not?

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:10.316
Without question.

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:11.017
I mean, and

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:12.218
he shouldn't be faulted for that.

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:13.653
I mean, this is a president

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:15.121
reasserting his authority

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:16.522
from the Oval Office

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:17.624
to the American people

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:19.125
about what he has done

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:21.160
and what his ideas are to go forward.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.895
This is what presidents do.

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:25.531
I think that it was as much of a

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:27.934
theory of the case for his campaign,

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:28.835
for his reelection

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:29.969
than anything we have heard.

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:32.071
We have largely seen a campaign video.

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:33.640
We've seen him to a couple addresses.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:34.941
But I think this laid out

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:36.342
in very stark terms

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:38.611
his view, his theory of the case, Erin.

00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:39.279
The question

00:04:39.279 --> 00:04:42.015
is, are Americans still listening

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:43.816
to President Biden?

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:45.652
The question is, are independents

00:04:45.652 --> 00:04:46.719
or even some of the Democrats

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:47.920
who supported him

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.255
still listening to the president

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:50.657
and to get the president's approval

00:04:50.657 --> 00:04:52.592
rating up from historic lows?

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:53.459
The White House knows

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:54.227
that they must win over

00:04:54.227 --> 00:04:54.961
some of the

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:57.030
very people who supported him,

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:57.997
some of the very people

00:04:57.997 --> 00:05:00.266
who generally have good feelings for him,

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:01.801
but are ready to sort of move

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:02.468
to something else.

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:03.870
So I think this was the beginning

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:05.938
of reasserting his command,

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:07.206
reasserting his

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:07.874
you know,

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:09.676
his control over Washington,

00:05:09.676 --> 00:05:10.109
showing, look,

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:11.477
I did work with both sides.

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:14.213
This is why you sent me to Washington

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.449
to get here in the most important part.

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:19.052
Are people still listening to Joe Biden?

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:20.119
And of course,

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:21.321
that's going to be the crucial question.

00:05:21.321 --> 00:05:21.688
Van.

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:22.822
I'll also say, you know,

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:23.656
when you when you hear this,

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:25.058
I understand you operate in the moment.

00:05:25.058 --> 00:05:26.726
The politics are about the moment

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:28.761
they're about, I protected you.

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:30.263
They're not about big picture.

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:31.531
But, Van, honestly,

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:33.166
some of this is frustrating, right? Okay.

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:34.567
Social Security's protected.

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:35.301
Social Security

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:37.537
benefits are going to be cut by 25%.

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:38.304
People are going to get less

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:40.406
than 80%, maybe 75% of what

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:41.207
they think

00:05:41.207 --> 00:05:43.376
they're going to get in just a few years.

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:43.776
Right.

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:45.278
Because something has to be done on

00:05:45.278 --> 00:05:46.112
Social Security.

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:47.580
So I get it. You seize the moment.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:48.247
I did nothing.

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:49.816
Now it doesn't take away

00:05:49.816 --> 00:05:50.350
the fact

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:51.918
that there are very huge decisions

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:53.152
that this country needs to make,

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:54.287
that the political system right

00:05:54.287 --> 00:05:55.254
now, frankly, completely

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:56.322
fails us at doing

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:58.858
I think you are correct.

00:05:58.858 --> 00:05:59.692
That's just the question is

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:01.194
do you want to use a debt,

00:06:01.194 --> 00:06:01.994
a debt

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:04.831
ceiling, hostage debate situation

00:06:04.831 --> 00:06:05.965
to resolve that stuff?

00:06:05.965 --> 00:06:06.566
I agree.

00:06:06.566 --> 00:06:08.568
There's you got to have stuff to do

00:06:08.568 --> 00:06:09.669
and you got to move stuff for it.

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:11.304
I just want to say, you know,

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:14.340
Joe Biden just keeps being Joe Biden.

00:06:15.141 --> 00:06:17.844
He just does the same Joe Biden thing

00:06:17.844 --> 00:06:19.112
and he keeps winning.

00:06:19.112 --> 00:06:21.347
And it's just it is kind of strange

00:06:21.681 --> 00:06:23.449
because he says, yeah, I like everybody.

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:24.717
We can all get along and Americans

00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:25.952
can always do great things.

00:06:25.952 --> 00:06:27.520
And you guys have a good night.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:28.921
And, you know, he's

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:30.857
it seems kind of corny,

00:06:30.857 --> 00:06:32.558
but then you look at the record

00:06:32.558 --> 00:06:33.659
of all the bills

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:34.994
that he's passed and the stuff

00:06:34.994 --> 00:06:36.062
he's done on climate stuff

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:37.096
he's done on infrastructure stuff

00:06:37.096 --> 00:06:38.431
he's done the CHIPS Act,

00:06:38.431 --> 00:06:39.999
you know, this debt ceiling thing behind.

00:06:39.999 --> 00:06:41.000
So there's just it's

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.368
I think for those of us

00:06:42.368 --> 00:06:43.803
who expect something new

00:06:43.803 --> 00:06:45.505
or dramatic or exciting,

00:06:45.505 --> 00:06:46.939
or interesting or different, he's

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:47.940
just like that old slugger.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:48.641
He just goes up there

00:06:48.641 --> 00:06:49.909
every time he hits a triple

00:06:49.909 --> 00:06:51.310
and then goes back to the dugout, hits

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:52.044
another triple goal.

00:06:52.044 --> 00:06:53.613
And you look at the scoreboard

00:06:53.613 --> 00:06:56.215
and he is doing pretty well.

00:06:56.215 --> 00:06:57.216
That said,

00:06:57.216 --> 00:06:58.351
there are big problems

00:06:58.351 --> 00:07:00.153
that are still not being addressed.

00:07:00.153 --> 00:07:02.321
If they ever do get addressed, it will be

00:07:02.355 --> 00:07:04.157
I think it looks like

00:07:04.157 --> 00:07:05.725
in the mode of a Joe Biden

00:07:05.725 --> 00:07:06.259
where you do

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:06.926
at the end of the day

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:07.360
with after

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:08.361
after all the nonsense,

00:07:08.361 --> 00:07:10.096
you get to a bipartisan consensus,

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:11.297
you get a big vote,

00:07:11.297 --> 00:07:12.698
everybody gets a little bit of love.

00:07:12.698 --> 00:07:14.066
Everybody gets go home with a cookie

00:07:14.066 --> 00:07:15.601
and a pat on the head from grandpa.

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:16.903
We do it all again next week.

00:07:16.903 --> 00:07:18.171
And you know, Michael, to you,

00:07:18.171 --> 00:07:18.604
to your point

00:07:18.604 --> 00:07:20.506
about an Oval Office address,

00:07:20.506 --> 00:07:21.841
maybe the reason he doesn't

00:07:21.841 --> 00:07:23.276
hasn't given one until tonight is

00:07:23.276 --> 00:07:25.044
it's not the best format for him.

00:07:25.044 --> 00:07:26.012
Let's just be honest, right?

00:07:26.012 --> 00:07:26.379
He's better

00:07:26.379 --> 00:07:28.381
when he's interacting with people.

00:07:28.381 --> 00:07:29.048
But he had

00:07:29.048 --> 00:07:30.817
you know, he delivered a speech

00:07:30.817 --> 00:07:32.251
and he had, you know, the moment sort

00:07:32.251 --> 00:07:32.952
of where he seemed to be

00:07:32.952 --> 00:07:33.853
the most animated

00:07:33.853 --> 00:07:35.087
you know, talking about his father.

00:07:35.087 --> 00:07:35.354
Right.

00:07:35.354 --> 00:07:36.189
His father saying,

00:07:36.189 --> 00:07:37.890
don't you tell me what you value.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.025
Show me your budget

00:07:39.025 --> 00:07:41.294
and I'll tell you what you value.

00:07:41.294 --> 00:07:43.629
There were moments where he was

00:07:43.629 --> 00:07:43.863
you know,

00:07:43.863 --> 00:07:45.731
as if there were people with him.

00:07:45.731 --> 00:07:49.035
Did he did he deliver in that regard,

00:07:49.035 --> 00:07:50.736
Michael, what he needs to

00:07:50.736 --> 00:07:52.004
or as everyone saying here,

00:07:52.004 --> 00:07:53.039
does it just not matter?

00:07:53.039 --> 00:07:54.574
Because people know you get what you

00:07:54.574 --> 00:07:56.342
get is a known quantity

00:07:58.511 --> 00:08:00.913
it was a fine set of remarks in my notes.

00:08:00.913 --> 00:08:03.049
I wrote a preview of coming attractions

00:08:03.049 --> 00:08:03.683
because now

00:08:03.683 --> 00:08:05.585
I have a slightly different take

00:08:05.585 --> 00:08:07.353
on the Republican side of the aisle.

00:08:07.353 --> 00:08:09.755
This campaign has gone from zero to 100

00:08:09.755 --> 00:08:11.591
in like no time.

00:08:11.591 --> 00:08:12.458
And I sense that he's

00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:14.760
champing at the bit to be heard

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.395
and that this is the way

00:08:16.395 --> 00:08:17.530
in which he's going to campaign

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:19.432
much like he stayed in Delaware.

00:08:19.432 --> 00:08:21.033
And I don't say that as a pejorative.

00:08:21.033 --> 00:08:22.668
We were in the midst of the pandemic,

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:23.603
but I think it's going to be

00:08:23.603 --> 00:08:26.439
an Oval Office Rose Garden strategy.

00:08:26.439 --> 00:08:27.173
And this is the way

00:08:27.173 --> 00:08:28.007
you're going to see him

00:08:28.007 --> 00:08:29.442
try to respond to that,

00:08:29.442 --> 00:08:30.710
which is said about him

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:32.011
by his Republican opponents

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:32.979
for the next several months.

